  "evidenceChain": [
    "NativeRoot uses Hebrew literal title/label keys with no tableName/bundle argument or Loc calls.",
    "PinkhaAnyNative Package has no resource declaration. Standalone NativeApp PBXResourcesBuildPhase file sets are empty; knownRegions/developmentRegion do not supply translations.",
    "Shared Anytype target explicit Resources phase has only InfoPlist.strings and asset/icon catalogs. Its actual synchronized groups are Sources, Video and Preview Content.",
    "Complete immutable Sources metadata contains only PinkhaSemanticAnchors.xcstrings and PinkhaTorahProperties.xcstrings. Their whole bodies are source-verified, are separate named tables, and contain none of these Hebrew keys. Video/Preview metadata supplies no string table.",
    "The actual English main Strings directory contains only InfoPlist.strings with five permission-description keys. That named InfoPlist table is not the default Text table.",
    "Loc has an en defaultLocalization and processes exactly Auth/UI/Workspace catalogs. Its generated resolver explicitly uses Bundle.module and named tables. NativeRoot does not invoke that resolver, and these package tables are not an implicit main/default lookup.",
    "The current project shell phases only register Git hooks and copy the Google services plist; no localization-table copy/generation phase is declared."
  ],
  "conclusion": "These declared inputs provide no English translation path for the current Hebrew default-table keys. Standard SwiftUI fallback therefore keeps those label keys Hebrew even when English is requested; the unnamed-Space String fallback is independently Hebrew. This is a source/resource conclusion, not a readback of a compiled English bundle.",
